# Fingerprints of findings that are KNOWN, RECORDED and already being dealt with.
#
# This file exists so that .gitleaks.toml does not have to. A gitleaks allowlist can silence
# a finding by matching the secret's literal text — and doing that commits the secret again,
# in the one file a reader trusts to be clean. A fingerprint pins commit + file + rule + line
# and names no value, which is the same outcome without the disclosure.
#
# Every entry below must say what it is, why it is tolerable now, and what closes it. An
# entry with no exit is an accepted leak wearing a suppression's clothes.
#
# See docs/architecture/00-SECURITY-IMMEDIATE.md and issue #27.

